## Fastest way: the AutoSkill CLI

```bash
pipx install autoskill-local          # once per machine (or: uv tool install autoskill-local)
autoskill login {{ ctx.server_url }}  # opens the browser to connect this machine
autoskill {{ "trial install" if ctx.trial else "install" }} {{ ctx.skill_name }}@{{ ctx.version }} --target {{ adapter.id }}
```

The CLI copies the skill into the right folder, registers the MCP servers below in `{{ adapter.mcp_config_path }}`,
asks you for the required environment values and stores them only in your agent's configuration.

